        "description": {
            "value": "<p><strong>Trigger</strong> You or an ally within 30 feet takes damage from a creature you can see.</p><hr /><p>You reverse the two events. The triggering creature takes @Damage[2d6[spirit]] damage, and the target of the trigger gains <strong>resistance equal to your level</strong> against the triggering damage.</p><hr /><p><strong>Heightened (+2)</strong> The damage increases by 1d6.</p><p><strong>Refined (9th)</strong> You additionally gain <strong>Licht Regen</strong>.</p><hr /><p><em>This is Bakud&#333; #81 with the damage reflected instead of absorbed, which is exactly what Antithesis does in canon.</em></p>"
